    "A program change on channel 10 changes nothing, because the rhythm part has no program.",
    "Bank select (CC0 and CC32) is ignored.",
    "The drum map is the factory rhythm key assignment printed in the owner's manual; a rhythm setup sent by SysEx can change it.",
    "Sound names follow Roland's printed sound lists (programs 65 to 128 from the MT-32 owner's manual, 1 to 64 from the CM-32L owner's manual, which has the same preset timbres), and the instrument's display may space them differently."
